exports[`help > lists the commands and the global options 1`] = `
"better-supabase v<version>
Typed Supabase: codegen, doctor, the SQL modules and project setup

Usage: better-supabase <command> [options]

Set up
  init        Writes better-supabase.config.ts, src/lib/supabase/index.ts and glue for the frameworks in package.json
  add         Adds blocks with what they require, a preset with --preset, existing tables with --adopt, or glue for an integration with --integration
  remove      Removes blocks: their config entries, their clients in lib/blocks.ts and the SQL files no other block needs
  table       Turns a per-table feature on or off with its @bsb tag in the table comment, in the schema file that creates the table
  upgrade     Brings the blocks' SQL up to the config and this release: upgrade steps for blocks behind, then every block's files
  blocks      Lists, shows and searches the blocks you can add, and decodes presets
  skills      Installs the Agent Skills that ship with this version of better-supabase
  completion  Prints the shell completion script for bash, zsh or fish, for both better-supabase and bsb

Generate
  gen        Writes the typed client from the database, then every other generated file the config sets up
  powersync  Writes PowerSync sync streams, the PowerSync schema and the publication migration for the blocks that sync offline
  spec       Writes, checks or validates the OpenAPI and other spec documents your defineApi() module renders

Local stack
  dev  Works with the local stack: its env file, commands run against it, its signing key and the stacks on this machine
  db   Runs SQL files and seeds against the database, backfills columns, prunes ended workflow runs, and diffs the declarative schema: the local stack by default, or the one in the connection string

Inspect
  doctor  Checks RLS, indexes, drift, auth config and env files; exits 1 on errors, or on warnings with --fail-on warning
  config  Prints the resolved config: the file it came from, the active environment and every option with its default, or the preset it names with --preset
  mcp     Serves the CLI to coding agents as an MCP server on stdio: read-only tools, and file writes with --allow-writes and the user's consent

Maintain
  migrate  Moves a project to a newer model: schema-first turns appTables into table files you own
  codemod  Rewrites imports, calls and config keys for renamed better-supabase APIs

Global options
  --cwd <dir>            Project directory
  --config <file>        Config file, relative to --cwd
  --env <name>           Config environment to apply ($env.<name> or $<name>). Defaults to $BETTER_SUPABASE_ENV, then ci when $CI is set
  --json                 Print one JSON document on stdout; errors as Problem Details. On by default in agent mode
  --agent <auto|yes|no>  Agent mode (JSON output, no prompts, consent for destructive work): auto detects a coding agent, yes or no decide. Defaults to $BETTER_SUPABASE_AGENT, then auto
  --confirm <token>      The token from a consent_required result, passed once the user agreed
  -y, --yes              Ask nothing; use the flags and the defaults
  --no-color             Print no colors, like $NO_COLOR
  --debug                Print stack traces, the commands the CLI runs, and timings on stderr
  -h, --help             Show help
  --version              Print the version

Run better-supabase <command> --help for a command's options.
Docs: https://bettersupabase.com/docs/cli
"
`;
